# core.autocrlf=true on Windows checks files out with CRLF, which breaks them on
# Linux: bash fails on a `\r` in a shebang or command, and Docker carries the
# `\r` into RUN lines. Everything here executes in a container or on a CI
# runner, so pin the whole tree to LF regardless of platform.
#
# A catch-all rather than a list of extensions: without one, a Windows checkout
# left every file in this repository looking modified from inside the
# devcontainer, which buries real changes in line-ending noise.
* text=auto eol=lf
